description: Active probes and the OT safety envelope
globs: internal/probe/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Before editing, read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §3 (Active probes) and §5 (OT safety controls), and `AGENTS.md` rules 7, 11 and 12.

- Every send acquires `probe.Budget`, which checks the policy, kill switch, excludes, budgets and per-target spacing. Never bypass it, and never send outside `platform.Transmitter`.
- Engines emit observations only (`arp_scan`, `icmp_scan`, `tcp_connect`, `udp_probe`, `identify_probe`). No reply means nothing, never offline.
- `scan plan` (`probe.Compute`) and `scan run` must agree on scope and refusals.
- Identification probes are opt-in, once per MAC (ADR 0011). A new payload-sending probe the contract does not already name needs a recorded decision before any code, interface or stub.
- Verify with `make check-all`; `TestActiveDiscovery` in `test/net` measures the budgets on the wire.
